% Two of a signature, a SHA-256 preimage and a HASH160 preimage
%
% The Logical English twin of a Bitcoin spending policy, written by the
% Miniscript translator (InsurLE2/migration/miniscript). Who can spend the
% coin, when, and why: each rule is one spending path of the policy.
%
% Source: the Bitcoin Core Miniscript tests
%         https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/src/test/miniscript_tests.cpp
%
% The source, as written (cut into lines of 100 characters: join them for the text):
%     thresh(2,c:pk_h(025cbdf0646e5db4eaa398f365f2ea7a0e3d419b7e0330e39ce92bddedcac4f9bc),s:sha256(e38990d
%     0c7fc009880a9c07c23842e886c6bbdc964ce6bdd5817ad357335ee6f),a:hash160(dd69735817e0e3f6f826a9238dc2e29
%     1184f0131))
%
% The source, laid out (keys and hashes by their role, <like this>):
%     thresh(2,
%       c:pk_h(<the key holder>),
%       s:sha256(<the payment secret>),
%       a:hash160(<the release secret>))
%
% The legend (role <- key or hash as written in the source):
%     the key holder     <- 025cbdf0646e5db4eaa398f365f2ea7a0e3d419b7e0330e39ce92bddedcac4f9bc
%     the payment secret <- e38990d0c7fc009880a9c07c23842e886c6bbdc964ce6bdd5817ad357335ee6f
%     the release secret <- dd69735817e0e3f6f826a9238dc2e291184f0131
%
% What it says (the spending policy, by BIP 379's semantics):
%     at least 2 of these 3:
%       a signature by the key holder
%       the preimage of the payment secret (sha256)
%       the preimage of the release secret (hash160)
%
% Try it in Minsc (the policy compiled to Miniscript, Script and an address,
% in the browser): the document "the policy in Minsc" below.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base hash_threshold includes these resources:
    temporal.

the templates are:
    the coin can be spent.
    the witness reveals the preimage of *a hash*; scenario element.
    the witness contains a signature by *a key*; scenario element.
    the condition *a condition* is met.
    the public key of *a key* is *a text*.
    the hash function of *a hash* is *a function*.
    the hash value of *a hash* is *a text*.

the knowledge base hash_threshold includes:

the Bitcoin Core Miniscript tests is published at "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/src/test/miniscript_tests.cpp".
the text of the Bitcoin Core Miniscript tests is at "sources/core_miniscript_tests.txt".

the policy in Minsc is published at "https://min.sc/#c=//%20Two%20of%20a%20signature,%20a%20SHA-256%20preimage%20and%20a%20HASH160%20preimage%0A//%20The%20Logical%20English%20twin's%20policy%20(InsurLE2/migration/miniscript).%0A$key_holder%20=%20025cbdf0646e5db4eaa398f365f2ea7a0e3d419b7e0330e39ce92bddedcac4f9bc;%20%20%20//%20the%20key%20holder%20(as%20in%20the%20source)%0A$payment_secret%20=%20e38990d0c7fc009880a9c07c23842e886c6bbdc964ce6bdd5817ad357335ee6f;%20%20%20//%20the%20payment%20secret,%20sha256%20(as%20in%20the%20source)%0A$release_secret%20=%20dd69735817e0e3f6f826a9238dc2e291184f0131;%20%20%20//%20the%20release%20secret,%20hash160%20(as%20in%20the%20source)%0A%0Athresh(2,pk($key_holder),sha256($payment_secret),hash160($release_secret))%0A".

% The keys and hashes of the policy, as the source writes them.
the public key of the key holder is "025cbdf0646e5db4eaa398f365f2ea7a0e3d419b7e0330e39ce92bddedcac4f9bc".

the hash function of the payment secret is sha256.

the hash function of the release secret is hash160.

the hash value of the payment secret is "e38990d0c7fc009880a9c07c23842e886c6bbdc964ce6bdd5817ad357335ee6f".

the hash value of the release secret is "dd69735817e0e3f6f826a9238dc2e291184f0131".

% The spending paths of the policy.
rule two_of_three with provenance the Bitcoin Core Miniscript tests,
        confer "thresh(2,c:pk_h(025cbdf0646e5db4eaa398f365f2ea7a0e3d419b7e0330e39ce92bddedcac4f9bc),s:sha256(e38990d0c7fc009880a9c07c23842e886c6bbdc964ce6bdd5817ad357335ee6f),a:hash160(dd69735817e0e3f6f826a9238dc2e291184f0131))":
the coin can be spent if
    a number N is the count of each C such that
        a condition C is in [the signature of the key holder, the preimage of the payment secret, the preimage of the release secret]
        and the condition C is met
    and N >= 2.

rule two_of_three_condition_1 with provenance the Bitcoin Core Miniscript tests,
        confer "thresh(2,c:pk_h(025cbdf0646e5db4eaa398f365f2ea7a0e3d419b7e0330e39ce92bddedcac4f9bc),s:sha256(e38990d0c7fc009880a9c07c23842e886c6bbdc964ce6bdd5817ad357335ee6f),a:hash160(dd69735817e0e3f6f826a9238dc2e291184f0131))":
the condition the signature of the key holder is met if
    the witness contains a signature by the key holder.

rule two_of_three_condition_2 with provenance the Bitcoin Core Miniscript tests,
        confer "thresh(2,c:pk_h(025cbdf0646e5db4eaa398f365f2ea7a0e3d419b7e0330e39ce92bddedcac4f9bc),s:sha256(e38990d0c7fc009880a9c07c23842e886c6bbdc964ce6bdd5817ad357335ee6f),a:hash160(dd69735817e0e3f6f826a9238dc2e291184f0131))":
the condition the preimage of the payment secret is met if
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret.

rule two_of_three_condition_3 with provenance the Bitcoin Core Miniscript tests,
        confer "thresh(2,c:pk_h(025cbdf0646e5db4eaa398f365f2ea7a0e3d419b7e0330e39ce92bddedcac4f9bc),s:sha256(e38990d0c7fc009880a9c07c23842e886c6bbdc964ce6bdd5817ad357335ee6f),a:hash160(dd69735817e0e3f6f826a9238dc2e291184f0131))":
the condition the preimage of the release secret is met if
    the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret.

scenario path_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 1 — the path needs: the preimage of the release secret, the preimage of the payment secret
    the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario path_1_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 1 without requirement 1 — the path needs: the preimage of the release secret, the preimage of the payment secret
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario path_1_without_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 1 without requirement 2 — the path needs: the preimage of the release secret, the preimage of the payment secret
    the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario path_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 2 — the path needs: the preimage of the release secret, a signature by the key holder
    the witness contains a signature by the key holder.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario path_2_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 2 without requirement 1 — the path needs: the preimage of the release secret, a signature by the key holder
    the witness contains a signature by the key holder.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario path_2_without_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 2 without requirement 2 — the path needs: the preimage of the release secret, a signature by the key holder
    the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario path_3 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 3 — the path needs: the preimage of the payment secret, a signature by the key holder
    the witness contains a signature by the key holder.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario path_3_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 3 without requirement 1 — the path needs: the preimage of the payment secret, a signature by the key holder
    the witness contains a signature by the key holder.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario path_3_without_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 3 without requirement 2 — the path needs: the preimage of the payment secret, a signature by the key holder
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario no_witness is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % an empty witness
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario flip_now is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, no delay passed
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret", "add: the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by the key holder", "add: the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by the key holder", "add: the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret"]].

scenario flip_after_delays is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, every delay passed
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret", "add: the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by the key holder", "add: the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by the key holder", "add: the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret"]].

scenario lost_the_key_holder is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of the key holder lost, everything else given
    the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret.
    the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the witness reveals the preimage of the payment secret"], ["remove: the witness reveals the preimage of the release secret"]].

query spendable is:
    the coin can be spent.

query flip_spend is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        the coin can be spent.

query flip_block is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        it is not the case that the coin can be spent.

query keys is:
    the public key of which key is which text.

query hash_functions is:
    the hash function of which hash is which function.

query hashes is:
    the hash value of which hash is which text.

the view custody explainer is:
    the title is "Who can spend this coin: Two of a signature, a SHA-256 preimage and a HASH160 preimage".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the facts about "the witness" are
        the witness reveals the preimage of a hash,
        the witness contains a signature by a key.
    the result is whether the coin can be spent.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the result can be flipped, as "What would let this coin be spent?".

